+## Governance Flow Choreography
+
+Governed work uses three explicit modes. Preserve exact-byte, owner, authority, risk,
+public/private, publication, Git, deployment, external-effect, executable-identity,
+and independent-review protections in every mode.
+
+1. **Preacceptance / no-effect** — validate the schema-first machine source, derive
+   human views deterministically, run every reachable declared consumer, collect all
+   blockers, and continue bounded environmental or mechanical evidence-only retries
+   automatically. Run-local evidence is the only permitted write. Mark a dependent
+   check `not_evaluable` with causal blockers; never call it PASS or omit it.
+2. **Human decision** — after rehearsal, freeze one immutable owner decision graph,
+   obtain independent review, emit at most one idempotent owner request for its digest,
+   and stop. Preparation, rehearsal, freeze, review, or request emission grants no
+   selection, admission, execution, publication, deployment, or external-effect authority.
+3. **Effectful execution** — after exact acceptance, selection, and admission, execute
+   only the accepted envelope and fail fast at the first effectful failure or real
+   governance blocker. Never execute a successor implicitly.
+
+The artifact chain is monotonic: source -> derived graph -> rehearsal -> freeze ->
+review -> request -> acceptance -> execution. A terminal outcome contract dominates
+local PASS receipts. `Bounded` means the smallest complete vertical slice that crosses
+every required real consumer and reaches the promised terminal boundary.
+
